Optical transport attribution
-----------------------------

CrumbBeam's LT fountain-code implementation and browser optical transport are
informed by and partially adapted from the MIT-licensed project:

  Decimen Optical Transfer
  https://github.com/bashalarmistalt/decimen-optical-transfer

Concepts and implementation lessons adapted or independently reimplemented for
CrumbBeam include:

- self-describing one-way screen-to-camera frames;
- deterministic robust-soliton LT frame selection;
- avoiding JavaScript Math.log divergence across browser engines;
- worker-based ZXing-WASM QR decoding;
- dropping frames while workers are busy;
- tracking received frames rather than solved blocks for progress;
- requiring a secure browser context for camera capture;
- demanding exact camera frame rate before falling back to ideal constraints.

CrumbBeam's CRUMB-specific envelope, validation, transport metadata,
authenticated encryption, SHA-256 verification, user interface, documentation,
and integration model are original to this repository.

